{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_15-41-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_15-41-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The leader appends each accepted command as a local log entry for its term (b-dispatch-logs), then each per-peer replication goroutine pushes AppendEntries and reports the highest index the peer has stored (b-leader-replicate). commitment.match/recalculate turn those per-voter match indexes into a quorum index, refusing to commit anything below the first index appended in the leader's term (b-commit-quorum). When the quorum index advances, the leader loop publishes the new commit index and applies the committed prefix (b-leader-commit-apply). The support is 'qualified' because a match index only counts after the follower's log has been shown to agree with the leader's up to the previous entry.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-dispatch-logs\",\n        \"b-leader-replicate\",\n        \"b-commit-quorum\",\n        \"b-leader-commit-apply\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-commit-quorum\",\n        \"f-log-prefix\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"SR-DISPATCH\",\n        \"SR-LEADER-LOOP\",\n        \"SR-REPLICATE\",\n        \"SR-STALE\",\n        \"SR-COMMITMENT\",\n        \"SR-PROCESS-LOGS\",\n        \"SR-APPEND-ENTRIES\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Authority is scoped to a term and to the voter set of the latest configuration. A follower that stops hearing a leader becomes a candidate (b-heartbeat-timeout); the candidate proposes and persists the next term and asks for votes, optionally after a pre-vote round (b-candidate-election, b-prevote), and becomes leader only on a quorum of current voters. Voters decide with term, membership, an already-persisted vote for the term, and log up-to-date-ness (b-vote-grant). A leader abandons the role when it observes a higher term or cannot contact a quorum of current voters (b-leader-stepdown), and it can hand the role over deliberately with a replicated-then-TimeoutNow transfer (b-leadership-transfer).\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-heartbeat-timeout\",\n        \"b-candidate-election\",\n        \"b-vote-grant\",\n        \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n        \"b-prevote\",\n        \"b-leadership-transfer\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-term-vote\",\n        \"f-leadership-validity\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"SR-RUN-FOLLOWER\",\n        \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\",\n        \"SR-ELECT\",\n        \"SR-PERSIST\",\n        \"SR-REQUEST-VOTE\",\n        \"SR-PREVOTE\",\n        \"SR-LEASE\",\n        \"SR-RUN-LEADER\",\n        \"SR-STALE\",\n        \"SR-TRANSFER-IMPL\",\n        \"SR-TRANSFER\",\n        \"SR-CAND-FLAG\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A1 and A2 meet on three sourced points. First, the term-start-index rule in the commitment makes the leader's own new-term entry a precondition for committing anything, so a server that merely won an election cannot commit an earlier leader's entries (b-commit-quorum / f-commit-quorum / f-term-vote). Second, the voter set that defines both a winning quorum and the commitment quorum comes from the latest configuration, so membership changes reshape eligibility and commitment together (b-config-change, b-candidate-election / f-config-membership). Third, a follower only counts as support after its log prefix has been shown to match the leader's, and that same AppendEntries handling carries the term/state transitions; losing the term (b-leader-stepdown) discards the commitment that the old term's support created, while a transfer pushes the target to the leader's last index before handing over. Old work is handled by failing every inflight future with ErrLeadershipLost on step-down, so pending client requests cannot be mistaken for applied decisions.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-commit-quorum\",\n        \"b-config-change\",\n        \"b-candidate-election\",\n        \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n        \"b-follower-append\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-commit-quorum\",\n        \"f-term-vote\",\n        \"f-config-membership\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"SR-COMMITMENT\",\n        \"SR-LEADER-LOOP\",\n        \"SR-NEXT-CONFIG\",\n        \"SR-CONFIG-CORE\",\n        \"SR-RUN-LEADER\",\n        \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\",\n        \"SR-ELECT\",\n        \"SR-PERSIST\",\n        \"SR-REQUEST-VOTE\",\n        \"SR-LEASE\",\n        \"SR-STALE\",\n        \"SR-APPEND-ENTRIES\",\n        \"SR-RPC-HB\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"The heartbeat fast path (Raft.processHeartbeat, installed by NewRaft and dispatched from NetworkTransport.handleConn) runs appendEntries off the main loop for pure heartbeats; the fields touched are atomic or lock-protected but the ordering against the main loop is unverified.\",\n      \"Raft.timeoutNow campaigns on the target without consulting the request term or sender.\",\n      \"The membership-change error path in appendConfigurationEntry continues to publish the new latest configuration and commitment after a StoreLogs failure that already set state Follower.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core lines are read end to end from the leader's append/commit path and from the follower/candidate/voter/step-down path, and their three concrete connections (term-start-index commitment rule, configuration-driven quorum, prefix-validated support with pending-work failure on step-down) are sourced. The remaining items are local anomalies rather than unexplained formation or authority transitions, so the overview is usable while those leads stay open.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"ca522834d5af4e33837e53c5fb699fe6\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"ca522834d5af4e33837e53c5fb699fe6\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2324b095ff754f44aaf76f68b45df0a1\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"needs_specific_evidence\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"source_review\",\n        \"question\": \"Is a heartbeat delivered through the transport fast path serialized with the main loop before it updates the receiver's term, state and believed leader, or can Raft.appendEntries run concurrently with runFollower/runCandidate on the same instance?\",\n        \"importance\": \"The single-writer premise for the authority context (state, currentTerm, leaderAddr/leaderID) is what the whole election and step-down reasoning rests on. If an off-thread heartbeat can mutate that context while the main loop is in the middle of a campaign or a term change, a race could leave a node believing in a different leader/term than its own state machine; the consequence is a wrong authority view rather than a memory-safety crash, so the impact is bounded but the premise matters.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-LEASE\",\n          \"SR-RUN-FOLLOWER\",\n          \"SR-APPEND-ENTRIES\",\n          \"SR-RPC-HB\",\n          \"SR-NET-HB\",\n          \"SR-HB-HANDLER\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [],\n        \"objects\": [],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"follower receiving leader heartbeats\",\n          \"candidate campaigning while a heartbeat from a known leader arrives\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"NetworkTransport.handleConn classifies a request as a pure heartbeat and calls heartbeatFn directly\",\n          \"Raft.processHeartbeat dispatches to Raft.appendEntries\",\n          \"a concurrent main-loop iteration of runFollower or runCandidate reads and writes the same authority context\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-heartbeat-timeout\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"f-leadership-validity\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"b-follower-append\": \"the off-thread path that actually applies the heartbeat's term/leader update\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"setState and setCurrentTerm use atomic stores and setLeader uses a mutex, so a pure heartbeat does not obviously produce a torn read of any single field\",\n          \"a pure heartbeat carries no entries, no previous-entry index and a zero leader commit index, so it skips the log, configuration and commit branches of appendEntries\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Which fields a pure heartbeat actually mutates on the receiver, and whether the existing atomic/locked access already provides the needed ordering\",\n          \"Whether the main loop can observe the update while it is inside runCandidate's vote tally rather than only at a select boundary\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 1,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Raft.appendEntries is documented as callable only from the main thread, yet NewRaft installs Raft.processHeartbeat (which calls appendEntries) as the transport heartbeat handler, and NetworkTransport.handleConn, started as a goroutine per connection, invokes that handler directly for pure heartbeats. That is a concrete, sourced difference in the authority-context path; bounding which fields a pure heartbeat actually mutates and whether the existing atomic/locked access already serializes them decides whether the comment is stale or the code unsafe.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"Combines the recovered core map with a first sourced Candidate on the authority-context path. The candidate is deliberately narrow: the library comments say Raft.appendEntries must only run on the main loop, yet the same function is installed as the transport heartbeat handler and is invoked from the per-connection goroutine, so the single-writer premise for term/state/leader updates is worth bounding before treating either line as protected.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null,\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"2324b095ff754f44aaf76f68b45df0a1\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-commit-quorum\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-COMMITMENT\",\n          \"SR-LEADER-LOOP\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether the quorum match index computed over an uncommitted latest configuration can exceed what the committed configuration would allow before that configuration commits.\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-leader-commit-apply\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-leader-commit-apply\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n          \"b-config-change\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-config-change\",\n          \"b-leader-commit-apply\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-term-vote\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-PERSIST\",\n          \"SR-REQUEST-VOTE\",\n          \"SR-ELECT\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\",\n          \"b-persist-authority\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-follower-append\",\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-follower-append\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n          \"b-persist-authority\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-log-prefix\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-APPEND-ENTRIES\",\n          \"SR-REPLICATE\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-leader-replicate\",\n          \"b-follower-append\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-fsm-apply\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-follower-append\",\n          \"b-fsm-apply\",\n          \"b-leader-replicate\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-config-membership\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-CONFIG-CORE\",\n          \"SR-NEXT-CONFIG\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-follower-append\",\n          \"b-snapshot-resync\",\n          \"b-config-change\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\",\n          \"b-prevote\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-commit-quorum\",\n          \"b-config-change\",\n          \"b-follower-append\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n          \"b-prevote\",\n          \"b-snapshot-resync\",\n          \"b-vote-grant\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-applied-prefix\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-FSM-APPLY\",\n          \"SR-LEADER-LOOP\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether the FSM itself persists its effect is application-owned and not established here.\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-leader-commit-apply\",\n          \"b-fsm-apply\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-client-future\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-client-future\",\n          \"b-fsm-apply\",\n          \"b-leader-commit-apply\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"f-leadership-validity\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-LEASE\",\n          \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\",\n          \"SR-TRANSFER\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"b-candidate-election\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"b-dispatch-logs\",\n          \"b-leader-replicate\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n          \"b-heartbeat-timeout\"\n        ],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-candidate-election\",\n          \"b-dispatch-logs\",\n          \"b-leader-replicate\",\n          \"b-leader-stepdown\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": [\n          \"2324b095ff754f44aaf76f68b45df0a1\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"paused_candidate_ids\": [],\n    \"behavior_unknowns\": [\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-commit-quorum\",\n        \"activity\": \"A1\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether the quorum match index under an uncommitted configuration can advance beyond what the committed configuration would permit before that configuration commits.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-COMMITMENT\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"the startIndex rule prevents a new leader from committing entries left by an earlier term on the strength of its own election\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-follower-append\",\n        \"activity\": \"A2\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"The heartbeat fast path calls this same function from the transport connection goroutine while the function is documented as main-thread only; whether the touched fields being atomic/locked makes that safe is not established here.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-APPEND-ENTRIES\",\n          \"SR-RPC-HB\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"the PrevLogEntry/PrevLogTerm check refuses to append behind a mismatch, and NoRetryBackoff tells the leader to regress cheaply\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-prevote\",\n        \"activity\": \"A2\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether treating missing pre-vote support as a granted vote can let a partitioned candidate believe it would win.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-PREVOTE\",\n          \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"avoiding a term increment unless a quorum would vote for the candidate\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-leadership-transfer\",\n        \"activity\": \"A2\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether a TimeoutNow is validated against the sender or the current term before it forces a campaign.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-TRANSFER-IMPL\",\n          \"SR-TRANSFER\",\n          \"SR-CAND-FLAG\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"the target ignores the outgoing leader's heartbeats only for its transfer campaign, and the flag is cleared when the campaign ends\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-config-change\",\n        \"activity\": \"A4\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether a StoreLogs failure during appendConfigurationEntry leaves the latest configuration and commitment already moved to the new membership while the node has stepped down.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-NEXT-CONFIG\",\n          \"SR-CONFIG-CORE\",\n          \"SR-RUN-LEADER\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"the change is only applied once the previous configuration is committed, preserving the one-uncommitted-configuration rule\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"behavior_id\": \"b-fsm-apply\",\n        \"activity\": \"A5\",\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether a configuration entry can be applied to the FSM while the corresponding latest configuration has been rolled back by a log truncation is not established here.\"\n        ],\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-FSM-APPLY\",\n          \"SR-PROCESS-LOGS\"\n        ],\n        \"protections\": [\n          \"single-threaded application order prevents concurrent Apply calls\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"surfaces\": [\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Raft.processHeartbeat\",\n        \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-follower-append\"\n        ],\n        \"reason\": \"The transport heartbeat fast path invokes this handler outside the main loop: NewRaft installs it with trans.SetHeartbeatHandler, and NetworkTransport.handleConn (started with 'go') calls the handler directly for pure heartbeats. Raft.appendEntries is documented as main-thread only. Whether the touched fields being atomic or lock-protected makes the off-thread heartbeat safe is not established here.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-RPC-HB\",\n          \"SR-NET-HB\",\n          \"SR-HB-HANDLER\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Raft.timeoutNow\",\n        \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"b-leadership-transfer\"\n        ],\n        \"reason\": \"Handles a TimeoutNowRequest by clearing the leader and campaigning; the request's term and sender are not consulted, which is recorded as an open premise of b-leadership-transfer.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-TRANSFER\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": false\n      },\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"Transport.SetHeartbeatHandler\",\n        \"disposition\": \"infrastructure\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Transport-level plumbing that decides whether a request is fast-pathed to the beacon handler or delivered on the consumer channel; it is not itself a consensus obligation.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-NET-HB\",\n          \"SR-HB-HANDLER\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": false\n      },\n      {\n        \"entry_point\": \"BootstrapCluster/RecoverCluster\",\n        \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n        \"behavior_ids\": [],\n        \"reason\": \"Initialization and disaster-recovery entry points have not been traced in this run and are kept as an unread boundary rather than assigned a responsibility.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"SR-NEWRAFT\"\n        ],\n        \"high_consequence\": false\n      }\n    ],\n    \"core_regions\": [\n      {\n        \"activity\": \"A1\",\n        \"entries\": [\n          {\n            \"class_id\": \"A1\",\n            \"applicability\": \"applicable\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement: a leader's new entries advance to committed and then to the FSM only when a quorum of the current voter set has stored them.\",\n            \"realization_summary\": \"Raft.dispatchLogs writes entries to the local LogStore and marks them inflight; one followerReplication goroutine per peer ships AppendEntries and reports the follower's match index; commitment.match/recalculate advance commitIndex under the term-start-index rule; the leaderLoop commit path applies the committed prefix.\",\n            \"entry_points\": [\n              \"Raft.Apply/ApplyLog/Barrier (applyCh)\",\n              \"Raft.dispatchLogs\",\n              \"Raft.replicate/replicateTo/updateLastAppended\",\n              \"commitment.match/recalculate\",\n              \"Raft.leaderLoop commitCh case + Raft.processLogs\"\n            ],\n            \"behavior_ids\": [\n              \"b-dispatch-logs\",\n              \"b-leader-replicate\",\n              \"b-commit-quorum\",\n              \"b-leader-commit-apply\"\n            ],\n            \"variants\": [\n              \"single-server fast path in verifyLeader\",\n              \"pipelined replication fallback\",\n              \"snapshot replication when the entry is compacted away\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"SR-DISPATCH\",\n              \"SR-REPLICATE\",\n              \"SR-COMMITMENT\",\n              \"SR-LEADER-LOOP\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Partial understanding; neither candidate labels nor object counts establish exhaustion\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"activity\": \"A2\",\n        \"entries\": [\n          {\n            \"class_id\": \"A2\",\n            \"applicability\": \"applicable\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority: terms, votes, the leader role and its removal, including leadership transfer.\",\n            \"realization_summary\": \"Followers time out heartbeats and become candidates; candidates pre-vote (optionally), increment and persist the term, request votes and win on a quorum; voters decide with term, log up-to-date-ness, prior-vote and configuration checks; leaders step down on newer terms or lease loss; a leader can hand over via TimeoutNow.\",\n            \"entry_points\": [\n              \"Raft.runFollower heartbeat timer\",\n              \"Raft.runCandidate/electSelf/preElectSelf\",\n              \"Raft.requestVote/requestPreVote\",\n              \"Raft.appendEntries/installSnapshot term handling\",\n              \"Raft.checkLeaderLease/handleStaleTerm\",\n              \"Raft.initiateLeadershipTransfer/leadershipTransfer/timeoutNow\"\n            ],\n            \"behavior_ids\": [\n              \"b-follower-append\",\n              \"b-heartbeat-timeout\",\n              \"b-candidate-election\",\n              \"b-vote-grant\",\n              \"b-prevote\",\n              \"b-leader-stepdown\",\n              \"b-leadership-transfer\"\n            ],\n            \"variants\": [\n              \"pre-vote enabled or disabled\",\n              \"leadership-transfer campaign skips pre-vote\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Whether the heartbeat fast path changes the authority-observation ordering relative to the main loop.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"SR-RUN-FOLLOWER\",\n              \"SR-RUN-CANDIDATE\",\n              \"SR-REQUEST-VOTE\",\n              \"SR-LEASE\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Partial understanding; neither candidate labels nor object counts establish exhaustion\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"capacity\": {\n    \"remaining\": {\n      \"agent_calls\": 38,\n      \"experiments\": 8,\n      \"audit_units\": 4,\n      \"semantic_reviews\": 6,\n      \"revisions\": 4\n    },\n    \"remaining_seconds\": 2062.2323711639983,\n    \"new_obligation\": true,\n    \"direct_execution\